A('## Honest notes / limits')
A(f"1. **Front-view chin-side jaw edge.** The visible jaw line (strongest light->dark step per column, Unity-like soft studio) sits about 9-10 mm ABOVE the plate's tone edge at |x| 20-30 mm (Micro1k: 4-6 mm); mean over |x| 20-60: Micro1k {fj['summary_x20_60']['Micro1k']['jaw_line_z_err_vs_plate_mean_mm']:.1f} mm -> Micro1l {fj['summary_x20_60']['Micro1l']['jaw_line_z_err_vs_plate_mean_mm']:.1f} mm (max {fj['summary_x20_60']['Micro1l']['jaw_line_z_err_vs_plate_max_mm']:.1f}). Cause: the crest stays ON the jaw on the mesh's natural border (Micro1k rule); the plate's edge there is stubble pigment 6-12 mm lower, and the jaw-underside OUTLINE geometry is within ~3 mm of the plate jaw line (min z at |x| 20/30/40/50/60: {fj['underside_outline_min_z_mm_at_x_20_30_40_50_60']['Micro1l']} vs plate {fj['plate_jaw_line_z_mm_at_x_20_30_40_50_60']}). Micro1k's edge there was weak (contrast 16-19 at |x| 20-30), so its smaller 'error' was partly a weak-edge artefact. Lever if Adnan wants the chin-side edge lower: lower the chin control points of `ARC_L` in `l_jaw.py` and/or the U-drop (`drop` 1.0 moves the step ~5 mm lower at the cost of +0.6 mm on the 3/4 chin-bottom contour; tested as `d10`, not shipped because the front and 3/4 plates disagree there).")
A(f"2. **Shading tilt.** Part of the edge definition is lighting-only (custom-normal tilt <= {sb['max_extra_tilt_deg']:.1f} deg on {sb['verts_gt_1deg']} vertices, FBX normals = Import so Unity shows it; a re-normalising importer setting would remove it). Geometric crest <= {jc['max_geometric_crest_mm']:.2f} mm.")
A("3. **Plates disagree** at the chin by 3-4 mm (front plate: lower, U-shaped; both 3/4 plates: smaller / higher chin). The 3/4 chin-bottom contour error rose by 0.3 mm on average (see table); front half-width and profile outlines improved.")
A("4. **Face_M changed (disclosed):** only the lip + seam paint strips (+256 verts, +472 tris); the brief preferred 0 move, the lips request makes it necessary because the strips must follow the new lip surface. Unity colour: `LipUp` base colour (.60,.38,.31) -> (.72,.48,.37) in `HeroBaseMaleFormProof.cs` (rollback copy in `baseline/`).")
A("5. **Not touched (known residuals, not in this brief):** the dark nasolabial line beside one nose wing, expression / smile, ears, eyes, brows, nape / pelvis, neck cage band z 1.40-1.44. Stubble stays a preview until the skin has UVs / a vertex-colour path.")
A("6. The eye-gate lines are my reading of the proof sheets; the numbers above are supporting measurements, not the gate.")
